# This repo is LF everywhere, and core.autocrlf=true on Windows will happily
# hand back CRLF on any checkout - including the implicit one a `git stash pop`
# does. Every source file here starts with `assert "\r\n" not in src`, so a
# stashed-and-restored file then fails its own edit script with no explanation.
# Pinning the working-tree ending removes the hazard rather than documenting it.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.stl binary
*.blend binary
*.blend1 binary
